  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Page No.# 1/3 vs The State Of Assam And Anr on 30 October, 2024 Author: Malasri Nandi Bench: Malasri Nandi Page No.# 1/3 GAHC010225342024 THE GAUHATI HIGH COURT (HIGH COURT OF ASSAM, NAGALAND, MIZORAM AND ARUNACHAL PRADESH) Case No. : Crl.Pet./1308/2024 R. VASUDEVAN AND ANR S/O RAMACHANDRA IYER, A RESIDENT OF VIJAYA NAGAR, VELECHERY CHENNAI, TAMIL NADU-600042. 2: V.N. SHIVA SHANKAR S/O V.R. NARAYANAN A RESIDENT OF OLD NO. 5 NEW NO. 9 2ND LINK STREET CIT COLONY MYLAPORE CHENAI TAMAL NADU INDIA -600004 VERSUS THE STATE OF ASSAM AND ANR REPRESENTED BY THE LD. PP, ASSAM 2:FOOD SAFETY OFFICER (IN THE OFFICE OF THE JOINT DIRECTOR OF HEALTH SERVICES TINSUKIA ASSA Advocate for the Petitioner : MR G KHANDELIA, MR. K DEKA Advocate for the Respondent : PP, ASSAM, Page No.# 1/3 vs The State Of Assam And Anr on 30 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/150858581/ 1 BEFORE HONOURABLE MRS. JUSTICE MALASRI NANDI Page No.# ORDER 30.10.2024 Heard Mr. K. N. Choudhury, learned Sr. counsel assisted by Mr. G. Khandelia, learned counsel for the petitioners.",
    "facts": "By this application under Section 528 of BNSS, the petitioner has prayed for quashing and setting aside the order dated 07.11.2019 for taking cognizance under Section 26(1), 26(2)(i) of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 and any subsequent order passed by the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Tinsukia in CR Case No. 95/2019. However, a copy of the petition along with the documents annexed thereto be furnished to him. It is further submitted that the petitioner No.1 resigned from the company on 16.08.2016 and petitioner No.2 had been retired from service on 22.06.2016.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
